Package: datadeposit
Type: Package
Title: Archive-Ready Data Deposits for Stata, R, Python, and Excel
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Eric A.", "Booth", email = "eric.a.booth@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Writes a deposit folder in the style of data archives such as ICPSR
    and Harvard Dataverse: the data as csv plus Stata, R, and optional Excel and
    SPSS copies; a codebook in Markdown, Excel, DDI Codebook 2.5, and Frictionless
    Data Package form; and setup scripts that rebuild the labelled data from the
    csv in Stata, R, and Python. Reads and writes Stata .dta files with their
    characteristics, notes, shared value label sets, label languages, and
    extended missing values, so survey item text is kept with the data.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://github.com/ericabooth/datadeposit
BugReports: https://github.com/ericabooth/datadeposit/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1)
Imports: jsonlite, stats, tools, utils
Suggests: haven, writexl, readxl, digest, testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.1
